m:** Doubtful. Its C$2.4B equity offering was pulled on 14 October, and Caldria Ratings put it on negative watch afterwards. A downgrade would raise its borrowing cost and could limit how much debt it can add.\n- **Pellham's response:** It plans to cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and resize its Q1 2027 tender. That suggests it expects funding to be tight and is trimming capex to fit, not replacing the equity with debt.\n- **Market conditions:** Utility bond spreads widened from 130bp in Q1 to 135bp in Q2 and 165bp in Q3 (+30bp in Q3). Debt is still available, but it is getting more expensive. Equity markets are less receptive.\n\n**What I couldn't see:** I didn't open the utility tender calendar, which holds the capex amounts. I also didn't open Pellham's market statement, so I don't have its debt capacity or planned bond issuance. That means I can't size the funding gap.\n\n**Implication for the grid-equipment question:** Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria, so its funding constraint is a real downside risk to 2027 order volumes. Norvane's access to debt supports its own orders.","ttft_ms":3460,"type":"result","duration_ms":31261,"uuid":"b3e9be50-d415-426a-8da0-75e78a555a5a","ttft_stream_ms":2233,"time_to_request_ms":64,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":17,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":5,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":14,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":56,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":207,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":133,"process_rss_mib_result":206,"